       "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
       "markdown": "A positioning statement template is an internal strategic guide that defines how your brand or product should be perceived relative to your competitors.\n\n> \"For **[target audience]** who **[statement of need or opportunity]** , the **[product or brand name]** is a **[product category]** that **[key benefit]** . Unlike **[primary competitive alternative]** , our product **[unique selling proposition / differentiation statement]**.\"\n\n\n\n---\n\n#### Core Elements of the Template\n\n- **Target Audience:** The specific market segment you serve.\n- **Need or Opportunity:** The pain point or goal your audience faces.\n- **Product Category:** The industry or market space where you compete.\n- **Key Benefit:** The primary value your product provides.\n- **Competitive Alternative:** The main rival or status quo.\n- **Unique Differentiation:** What sets you apart from the competition.\n\n\n\n---\n\n#### Example in Practice\nFor a practical illustration like the TecCarry laptop bag example\u2014combining style and functionality for busy professionals\u2014you can find the full application and wording in the referenced materials.Learn more about building your brand framework through the [Harvard Business School Online Guide](https://online.hbs.edu/blog/post/brand-positioning-statement) or explore practical examples on [Zendesk](https://www.zendesk.com/blog/sales/sales-and-marketing/positioning-statement-examples/).If you'd like, share:\n\n- **What product or service** you are building\n- **Who your main customers** are\n- **What makes you different** from competitors\n\nI can help you draft a custom positioning statement for your brand.",
